From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 04:42:25 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] wordcraft-web: open a recovered document unsaved; one
 autosave writer

Phase 6 WP12 recovery (docs/phase6/lifecycle.md). `wordcraft:open { dirty: true }` opens the document with unsaved changes: the parent
hands back a `wordcraft:autosave` it kept after the page died (WebGL context loss, a killed or crashed renderer), so the document stays
marked unsaved, keeps its leave-page guard and keeps being autosaved. The autosave bytes come from `office_overlay::autosave_bytes`, the
writer, password and export options File > Save uses, so a recovery keeps what a Save keeps. Test: an opened docx with a picture, edited,
gives the same picture part in the autosave payload and in an explicit Save (`autosave_and_save_keep_the_picture_of_an_opened_document`).
